Z||000000||ezsurf||06-14-99||07:52 PM||||<br>I'm trying to get all the parts from my 2.8 back in the car after the engine rebuild.  The crossover tube has a horseshoe cutout on the end of a bracket attached to the tube.  It looks like it rests on a bolt, but I'm having a hard time figuring out where this bolt is supposed to be.  I haven't been able to find a picture of it in the Helm manual anywhere.  I sure could use a detailed description of where this thing mounts. 
Z||000001||PaUL||06-15-99||05:43 PM||||Are you talking about the exhaust or the coolant pipe? The coolant pipe has a bracket that bolts on to another bracket thats bolted to the trans.
Z||000002||ezsurf||06-15-99||06:05 PM||||PaUL,<br>I'm talking about the cooling tube.  Although, I believe you have answered the question.  It bolts onto another bracket that bolts to the transmission.  I'll look for a suitable location in that area.  You said that it bolts to another bracket, then to the transmission.  What does this other bracket go to?  I would have to say that it is probably the shift cables, but I'm pulling this from memory.  Hopefully I can piece it together.  Any additional info would be helpful.  Thanks.
Z||000003||ezsurf||06-15-99||07:49 PM||||PaUl,<br>I found where the tube mounts.  It seems incredibly easy once you find the right bolt.  But, you can't see it from underneath, and if your not looking down on it from directly above, you'll never see it.  Thanks again.
